.TH "PB-ENV-VAULT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-vault - Create, list and delete named ENV vaults that recipes read


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env vault [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
A named vault is a set of ENV values with its own key, for example canary-env. Members
of the workspace read it with their ENV keys, and machines paired from a recipe whose
[env] vaults lists it read it with the recipe's token, with nobody online. Set values
with pb env set <name> --vault <vault>\&.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for vault


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-vault-create(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-vault-delete(1)\fP, \fBpb-env-vault-list(1)\fP
